From f01e0b782747076cb18d6c9f7952bcc358ee87e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chevydan6 <339888127+chevydan6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:20:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] agp_gart: release the backend if aperture metadata allocation
 fails

Check the nothrow Aperture allocation before calling InitCheck. If metadata allocation fails after backend creation, delete that backend while its module reference is held, then drop the reference and return B_NO_MEMORY without inserting a registry object.

Thirteen production-manager host cases pass with ASAN/UBSAN and no exceptions or RTTI, including class-specific allocation failure, init failure, normal creation, retained unmap and guarded reopen. The baseline reaches a sanitizer-detected null pointer member access on metadata OOM. Native compilation remains pending.

Assisted-by: Codex
Signed-off-by: chevydan6 <339888127+chevydan6@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/agp_gart/agp_gart.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/agp_gart/agp_gart.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/agp_gart/agp_gart.cpp
index 96134f6b..44fa9fbc 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/agp_gart/agp_gart.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/bus_managers/agp_gart/agp_gart.cpp
@@ -1016,6 +1016,12 @@ map_aperture(uint8 bus, uint8 device, uint8 function, size_t size,
 			}
 
 			aperture = new(std::nothrow) Aperture(module, privateAperture);
+			if (aperture == NULL) {
+				module->delete_aperture(privateAperture);
+				put_module(name);
+				status = B_NO_MEMORY;
+				break;
+			}
 			status = aperture->InitCheck();
 			if (status == B_OK) {
 				if (_apertureBase != NULL)
